 { The next example shows the idea of one single diagonal in the hands of the defending side.Black's position is unpleasant, but salvation was just around the corner. } 1... { -KEY- } Bd5 $1 { Installing the bishop on a diagonal where it will control both enemy passed pawns. } ( { Instead, the game went } 1... Kb7 $2 2. Ke6 $1 Be8 3. f6 Kc6 4. d5 Kc7 5. Ke7 { and, unable to cope with the white pawns, Black resigned. } ) 
2. Ke5 ( { After } 2. Ke7 Kb6 3. f6 $2 Kc6 { White even loses, since } 4. f7 { runs into } Bxf7 5. Kxf7 Kd5 ) 
